-- title:
--   The relation generated by Definition 1 (unanimous order, proof device)
-- statement:
--   For the type $\theta_i$ of negotiator $i$, this is the relation on bundles with one edge from $(x,y)$ to $(x',y')$ for each instance of Definition 1: a monotonicity instance, a deal-breakers instance, or a logrolling instance. Its reflexive-transitive closure is the comparison the proof of Theorem 1 calls "unambiguous": one bundle is ranked at least as high as the other at every consistent ordering.
--
--   It is used by the richness milestone and does not occur in Theorem 1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** It is an inductive relation with three constructors, mirroring the three conditions of Definition 1.
-- source:
--   Kesten, Özyurt, Efficient and Incentive Compatible Mediation: An Ordinal Market Design Approach, working paper, 4 October 2018, Definition 1, p.13, and proof of Theorem 1, pp.28–29, 31–34

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MultiIssueMediation_ConsistentOrdering

namespace MultiIssueMediation

/-- The relation generated on bundles by the instances of Definition 1 i, ii, iii for the type `t`
of negotiator `i` (working paper of 4 October 2018, Definition 1, p.13). Its reflexive-transitive
closure is the unanimous order of the proof of Theorem 1: the comparisons the page calls
"unambiguously" ranked (pp.28–29, 31–34).

**Formalization Note.** This relation is a device of the milestones and does not occur in
Theorem 1. -/
inductive UnanimousStep {m : ℕ} (i : Negotiator) (t : Fin m) : Bundle m → Bundle m → Prop
  | monotone (x x' y y' : Option (Fin m)) (hne : (x, y) ≠ (x', y'))
      (hx : issueXPrefers i t x x' ∨ x = x') (hy : issueYPrefers i y y' ∨ y = y') :
      UnanimousStep i t (x, y) (x', y')
  | dealBreaker (x x' y y' : Option (Fin m)) (hy : y ≠ none) (hy' : y' ≠ none)
      (hx : x ∈ acceptable i t ∨ x = none) (hx' : x' ∉ acceptable i t) (hne : x ≠ x') :
      UnanimousStep i t (x, y) (x', y')
  | logrolling (x x' : Option (Fin m)) (hx : x ∈ acceptable i t) (hx' : x' ∈ acceptable i t)
      (hlt : issueXPrefers i t x x') :
      UnanimousStep i t (x', logroll x') (x, logroll x)

end MultiIssueMediation


